    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        104.19673156738281,
        527.4215698242188,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "national tuberculosis programmes on the management of tuberculosis in children (second edition) (8) .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        120.19074249267578,
        527.4156494140625,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "Treatment may require dose adjustment to reconcile the effect of age and possible toxicity in young",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        133.3907012939453,
        527.4192504882812,
        147.8336944580078
      ],
      "text": "infants. The decision to adjust doses should be taken by a clinician experienced in the management",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        146.59071350097656,
        147.90130615234375,
        161.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "of paediatric TB.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        168.11862182617188,
        527.43701171875,
        182.7376251220703
      ],
      "text": "Children treated for TB in the past two years: Given the increased risk of treatment failure and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        181.49464416503906,
        527.3925170898438,
        195.93763732910156
      ],
      "text": "of drug resistance, children and adolescents treated in the preceding two years were not eligible for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.69459533691406,
        524.2785034179688,
        209.13758850097656
      ],
      "text": "inclusion in the SHINE trial; they should be treated with the 6-month treatment regimen (2HRZ(E)/4HR).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.948027610778809,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        222.48793029785156,
        337.54132080078125,
        243.36793518066406
      ],
      "text": "5.1.3. Implementation considerations",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 16.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        249.39578247070312,
        527.4204711914062,
        264.0148010253906
      ],
      "text": "Assessing severity of disease : The feasibility of assessing the severity of TB disease, particularly in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        262.77178955078125,
        527.5520629882812,
        277.2148132324219
      ],
      "text": "settings without access to CXR or capacity for CXR interpretation and WHO-recommended diagnostic",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97126293182373,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        275.9718017578125,
        527.4265747070312,
        290.4148254394531
      ],
      "text": "tests was identified as a major implementation consideration. Chest radiography was identified by",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        289.17169189453125,
        527.4124145507812,
        303.6147155761719
      ],
      "text": "the GDG as a critical tool to evaluate the severity of intrathoracic disease. As indicated under the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        302.3717041015625,
        527.453125,
        316.8147277832031
      ],
      "text": "recommendation remarks, non-severe intrathoracic or PTB disease refers to: intrathoracic lymph",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        315.57171630859375,
        527.5243530273438,
        330.0147399902344
      ],
      "text": "node TB without airway obstruction; uncomplicated TB pleural effusion or paucibacillary, non-cavitary",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97216510772705,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        328.7716979980469,
        527.2308959960938,
        343.2147216796875
      ],
      "text": "disease confined to one lobe of the lungs and without a miliary pattern. Extensive or advanced",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        341.9717102050781,
        527.4058227539062,
        356.41473388671875
      ],
      "text": "disease in children under 15 years of age is usually defined by the presence of cavities or bilateral",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        352.377685546875,
        527.4427490234375,
        369.6147155761719
      ],
      "text": "(61) disease on CXR  . NTPs are encouraged to scale up access to quality CXR and provide training to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        368.3717041015625,
        527.44970703125,
        382.8147277832031
      ],
      "text": "health care providers in its interpretation. Out-of-pocket expenses for CXR pose a potential barrier",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        381.57171630859375,
        527.4003295898438,
        396.0147399902344
      ],
      "text": "to TB diagnosis and access to shorter regimen for eligible children and young adolescents. In the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        394.7716979980469,
        527.3903198242188,
        409.2147216796875
      ],
      "text": "SHINE trial, children who were Xpert MTB/RIF positive, but sputum smear-negative were eligible for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        407.9717102050781,
        527.4310913085938,
        422.41473388671875
      ],
      "text": "inclusion. The 85 children (7%) who were Xpert MTB/RIF positive (45 in the 4-month arm and 40 in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        421.17169189453125,
        438.7920227050781,
        435.6147155761719
      ],
      "text": "the 6-month arm), had very low or low semi-quantitative Xpert MTB/RIF results.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        440.08172607421875,
        527.4386596679688,
        457.3187255859375
      ],
      "text": "Operational handbook on the management of  Detailed implementation guidance is provided in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        453.2816162109375,
        527.4558715820312,
        470.51861572265625
      ],
      "text": "tuberculosis in children and adolescents , taking into consideration differences in the health care system",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.972816467285156,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        469.27569580078125,
        527.4322509765625,
        483.7187194824219
      ],
      "text": "and country context, including the availability of diagnostic tools to make a diagnosis and to assess",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        482.4757080078125,
        527.4201049804688,
        496.9187316894531
      ],
      "text": "disease severity. While access to CXR is an important implementation consideration, it should not be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        495.67572021484375,
        527.4599609375,
        510.1187438964844
      ],
      "text": "a barrier for children and adolescents in lower resourced settings to benefit from the shorter regimen.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.979931831359863,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        508.875732421875,
        527.4376220703125,
        523.3187255859375
      ],
      "text": "The implementation guidance in the operational handbook comprises criteria for assessing disease",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        522.0755615234375,
        527.4356079101562,
        536.5185546875
      ],
      "text": "severity, including clinical criteria in the absence of CXR or rapid diagnostics or other bacteriological",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        535.2756958007812,
        527.4344482421875,
        549.7186889648438
      ],
      "text": "tests, to determine eligibility for the shorter regimen. Children with Xpert MTB/RIF or Ultra results",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        548.4757080078125,
        527.4574584960938,
        562.918701171875
      ],
      "text": "that are trace, very low or low, who meet radiographical or clinical criteria for non-severe TB, can be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        561.6757202148438,
        232.73550415039062,
        576.1187133789062
      ],
      "text": "treated with the 4-month regimen.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        583.2036743164062,
        527.531494140625,
        597.8226318359375
      ],
      "text": "Continuum between TB infection and disease : An additional implementation consideration is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        596.57958984375,
        527.3914184570312,
        611.0225830078125
      ],
      "text": "the concept that a continuum exists between TB infection, non-severe and more severe forms of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        609.7796020507812,
        527.4013061523438,
        624.2225952148438
      ],
      "text": "TB disease in children. Shorter treatment regimens for drug-susceptible TB are now very similar to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        622.9796142578125,
        527.4356689453125,
        637.422607421875
      ],
      "text": "recently recommended shorter regimens for the treatment of TB infection, in terms of duration and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        636.1796264648438,
        527.314697265625,
        650.6226196289062
      ],
      "text": "composition, in particular the regimen that consists of 3 months of daily isoniazid and rifampicin",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        646.5856323242188,
        527.4269409179688,
        663.8226318359375
      ],
      "text": "(14) (3HR)  . This implies that incorrectly diagnosing a child who has TB infection as having non-severe",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        662.57958984375,
        287.41839599609375,
        677.0225830078125
      ],
      "text": "TB disease may not have severe consequences.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        684.1075439453125,
        527.4454956054688,
        698.7265014648438
      ],
      "text": "Contact investigation : Another implementation consideration is the scale-up of contact investigation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 10.966448783874512,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        697.4835205078125,
        527.4650268554688,
        711.926513671875
      ],
      "text": "approaches, which can improve early identification of children with non-severe disease who may",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        710.6834716796875,
        234.60440063476562,
        725.12646484375
      ],
      "text": "benefit from the 4-month regimen.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        732.21142578125,
        524.3312377929688,
        746.8303833007812
      ],
      "text": "Use of ethambutol in the intensive phase of treatment : Children and young adolescents with non-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 10.974520683288574,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        745.5875244140625,
        527.1990966796875,
        760.030517578125
      ],
      "text": "severe TB who live in settings with low HIV prevalence or a low prevalence of isoniazid resistance and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.99484920501709,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        758.7874755859375,
        527.45751953125,
        773.23046875
      ],
      "text": "those who are HIV negative can be treated with a three-drug regimen (HRZ) for 2 months, followed",
